        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "# Feature queries\n\nA panel often mixes two kinds of query: the **measurements** you are charting, and **reference queries** that only supply values to draw against (spec limits, a nominal target, limits looked up from a database). Reference series are still real time series, so by default the panel treats them as process data: they get their own row in the statistics table, with a meaningless Mean, Std Dev and Cp/Cpk.\n\nThe **Feature queries** option (panel editor → **SPC** section) marks queries as reference-only. Declared refIds are dropped from the statistics table, from the CSV export, and from the series numbering that computed control lines (Mean/LCL/UCL/±σ) index into. They are still drawn on the chart — that is the point of a reference series.\n\n> Note: a reference query that returns **no time field** (a plain lookup table such as `name,lsl,usl,nominal`) is already skipped automatically, because the panel only tabulates frames it can plot. Feature queries are what you need when the reference data *is* a time series, as below.\n\n## Queries\n\n| refId | Alias | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | `Bore diameter` | 24 measurements, process centred near 10.00 |\n| B | `LSL spec` | reference series, constant 9.85 |\n| C | `USL spec` | reference series, constant 10.15 |\n\n## What to verify\n\n1. **Left panel** (`Feature queries` empty): the statistics table has **three rows** — `Bore diameter`, `LSL spec`, `USL spec`. The two spec rows report a Std Dev of ~0 and no usable Cp/Cpk — they describe a constant, not a process. This is the state reported in issue #65.\n2. **Right panel** (`Feature queries` = B, C): the statistics table has **one row**, `Bore diameter`. Its n, Mean, Std Dev, Min, Max, LCL/UCL and Cp/Cpk are unchanged from the left panel — excluding the reference queries changes which rows appear, never the process numbers.\n3. **Both panels** draw the same three lines plus the same Mean/LCL/UCL control lines: the reference series stay visible.\n4. Open the right panel's editor: **SPC → Feature queries** is a multi-select listing A, B, C. Before the fix this option did not exist in the UI at all.\n5. Right-click each panel → **Download CSV**: the left export contains the two spec series, the right one does not.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "2.4.0",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
